    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Taylor Ward** stands as our highest-value asset with a 71.46 efficiency score. He benefits from a potent combination of a high-ceiling matchup against V\u00e1squez (xERA 4.89) and a significant park-factor boost that elevates his raw projection. Following closely, **Gleyber Torres** (67.52) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.72) provide our most reliable production; **Gleyber Torres** is capitalizing on a favorable platoon edge against a lefty, while **Geraldo Perdomo** leverages the favorable SP skill gap against Lowder. We are also leaning into **Gavin Sheets** (63.36) and **Jonathan Aranda** (63.75), both of whom see their scores buoyed by optimal lineup positioning and positive park dynamics, making them high-priority starts for our daily offensive output.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Matt Chapman**, who finished with a 44.81 score\u2014narrowly missing the cut. While he offers reliable defensive utility, his lower spot in the order compared to our starters and the neutral impact of the park caused him to lose out to the upside of **Gavin Sheets**. Conversely, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a \"must-start\" despite a lower score (57.43) resulting from a brutal matchup against the elite Skubal. Even with the SP skill penalty, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** provides too much categorical floor to move to the pine. We are closely monitoring the status of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains sidelined on the IL, and we continue to exercise caution with **Luis Arraez** and **Jung Hoo Lee**, both of whom face a challenging matchup against Brown, making their contributions volatile as we chase those critical, scarce stolen bases.",
